Error [E0920]: a function can't be both `#Inline` and `#InlineAlways`
  --> tests/ui/inline_conflicting_markers.jet:3:9
    |
  3 | #Inline #InlineAlways fn quad(x: Int) -> Int {
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `#Inline` is a soft hint the compiler may ignore; `#InlineAlways` is a checked promise it must honor or reject — one declaration can't carry both meanings.
 Fix: keep one: `#Inline` to suggest inlining, `#InlineAlways` to require it.
